Int64 over TEXT affinity, x > 2 must keep the row storing text 10:
10
Int64 over INTEGER affinity stays pushed down and correct:
10
String over INTEGER affinity, num_s < \'2\' must keep the row storing 10:
10
String with NOCASE collation, s > \'B\' must keep \'a\' (byte-wise order):
a
String with RTRIM collation, r > \'a\' must keep \'a \' (trailing space is significant):
a 	2
String over plain TEXT (BINARY collation) stays pushed down and correct:
a
View columns have no affinity, x > 2 must keep the row storing text 10:
10
Query: SELECT "n" FROM "t" WHERE "n" > 2
Query: SELECT "plain" FROM "t" WHERE "plain" > 'B'
Query: SELECT "x" FROM "t"
